        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "0b4aa5cc4bbd87776f01e2776dae80ebe80d715a",
            "parents": [
                "4bf3ed840f13c31720ffa7c255942f3836402f4f"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/52/79052/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "createdOn": 1743502413,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Yang",
                "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 189,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we really need a vector to track failure? We don't seem to be actually consuming the entries of the vector other than as a count."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 189,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Currently, the content of the vector is indeed not being used; it is only utilized to determine failure and for potential future use.\nCould you please suggest how we might modify it?\nThank you very much for your advice!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 189,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> Could you please suggest how we might modify it?\n\nIf we're not using it, don't add it?\n\n>  it is only utilized to determine failure and for potential future use.\n\nAdd it to a commit when that future comes."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 189,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 238,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "How does the caller fetch this information?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 238,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I believe the caller currently does not specifically handle this information.\nOnly a PLDM ERROR return code is provided to the upper layer through [discoverMctpTerminus], and there is no differentiated handling for SUCCESS and ERROR.\n\n[discoverMctpTerminus]: https://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/f264c08d50359f68e90dfeb22c3b4cb62d198c66/platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp#L157"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 240,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we fail only if none of the terminii can be discovered?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/terminus_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 240,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I am following the original approach, where an ERROR is determined if any terminus discovery fails.\nI believe this should be decided based on how PLDM ERRORs are handled.\nIf error handling is done on a per-mctpinfo basis, then I think an ERROR should be determined if any terminus discovery fails.\nBut currently, there is no handling in place for this aspect."
                }
            ],
